# Dentrix Clone UI - AI Assistant Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Dentrix clone UI built with Next.js 15, featuring an integrated Voice AI workflow for clinical note-taking. The project demonstrates real-time speech-to-text transcription using Deepgram API with a clean, modular React architecture.

## Technology Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 with App Router
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS + Radix UI components
- **Speech-to-Text**: Deepgram SDK (@deepgram/sdk)
- **AI Integration**: Vercel AI SDK (@ai-sdk/google, @ai-sdk/react, ai)
- **Audio**: Web MediaRecorder API + MediaStream API
- **State Management**: React Context API + Custom Hooks

## Architecture Principles

### File Organization
- **Peer Components**: Create separate files for complex components instead of inlining
- **Custom Hooks**: Extract business logic into reusable hooks (e.g., `useVoiceTranscription`)
- **Context Providers**: Use React Context for global state (Deepgram, Microphone)
- **Component Composition**: Break down complex UIs into focused, single-responsibility components

### Directory Structure
```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router pages
│   ├── context/           # Global Context Providers
│   └── components/        # App-specific components
├── components/            # Shared/reusable components
│   ├── ui/               # Base UI components (Radix)
│   └── voiceai/          # Voice AI workflow components
│       ├── components/   # Peer components
│       ├── hooks/        # Custom hooks
│       └── types.ts      # Type definitions
└── lib/                  # Utilities and helpers
```

## 📍 **File Placement & Configuration:**

1. **Place at project root**: `/Users/accelerator/Documents/experiments/dentrix-clone-ui/.cursorrules`
2. **No configuration needed**: Cursor automatically reads `.cursorrules` files
3. **File format**: Plain text (no extension needed, but `.cursorrules` is the convention)

